{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfTyGVAa7e5NLf72fpxLZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've drafted the acceptance contract for work item 20260908T113226. Key decisions reflected:\n\n- **Scope** is bounded to the plan's four files: the substantive `harness/claude_account_cli.py` change, its enforcing tests in `tests/unit/test_claude_account_cli.py`, the `RUNBOOK.md` correction (concern C1), and the mandated `releases/_next/*.md` note the CI gate requires.\n- **Deterministic criteria** use the manifest's declared verification command plus focused, non-vacuous checks (adapter tests, the token-convention `test_usage.py` that must stay green, and a `grep` proving the release note's Type line — which fails at base and passes after the change).\n- **One `DECISION:`** entry (per-model granularity: details-dict vs a SCHEMA_VERSION bump), written on the plan's details-dict option and naming every section each option would change.\n- Remaining unknowns kept as `ASSUMPTION:`/`GAP:` (CLI field names, helper-model shape), and the ADR-018/request conflict recorded as resolved (superseded by ADR-019 per the T1 review), so no new ADR is in scope.\n- Compatibility obligations (ADR-005 telemetry-never-fails, ADR-006 cache regression, ADR-007 live tier never a PR gate, ADR-019 no-credential-leak, and the release-notes gate) and failure semantics are preserved."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10515,"cache_read_input_tokens":53521,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10515},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4073920a-6e88-415b-bd1c-ffd89d1c4ab1","uuid":"9cde7d3b-72b8-4724-bfb1-79b66b08220a","request_id":"req_011CfTyGToxkhRvTvFGxYPmV"}
